1
00:00:06,632 --> 00:00:09,468
<i>Welcome to the exile zone.</i>

2
00:00:10,052 --> 00:00:11,637
No way. You've been sleeping here?

3
00:00:11,720 --> 00:00:13,013
I'm the keeper of this place's history.

4
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:17,768
All these pictures are here
to help us understand these two puzzles.

5
00:00:17,851 --> 00:00:19,436
"When the bird calls out six times,

6
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:21,522
you cover the sun."

7
00:00:21,605 --> 00:00:23,357
And "When day turns to night,

8
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:25,234
you can see the path."

9
00:00:25,317 --> 00:00:26,944
What could this game be?

10
00:00:27,027 --> 00:00:28,445
Let's get all the Korean sorted out first.

11
00:00:28,528 --> 00:00:30,739
Should we flip it
and try to read the characters?

12
00:00:30,822 --> 00:00:32,241
-"God's test…"
-"Test…"

13
00:00:32,324 --> 00:00:34,576
-"If you pass it,
-"If you pass it,

14
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:36,203
-you can survive."
-you can live."

15
00:00:36,286 --> 00:00:38,455
So basically, we either have to
survive the death matches

16
00:00:38,539 --> 00:00:40,999
or solve this and take that path.

17
00:00:41,083 --> 00:00:42,918
<i>The third exile zone match is</i>

18
00:00:43,001 --> 00:00:44,378
<i>Secret Code.</i>

19
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:46,463
<i>-Farewell, Shindong.</i>
-Good luck.

20
00:00:46,546 --> 00:00:49,174
Starting today,
this is the prison alliance.

21
00:00:49,258 --> 00:00:51,551
We stick together until the end.
All the way to the finals.

22
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:53,512
No weak thinking.

23
00:00:53,595 --> 00:00:55,055
Kill or be killed.

24
00:00:55,138 --> 00:00:58,016
<i>Today's main match is Gem Black Market.</i>

25
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,227
John Park,
you are Oh Hyun-min's secret friend.

26
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:01,687
I can totally screw him over.

27
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:03,313
Either dodge the bombs
and score points, or…

28
00:01:03,397 --> 00:01:05,983
It'll be worth it
if we can eliminate Hyun-min.

29
00:01:06,066 --> 00:01:08,068
Hyun-min, we only need to
funnel points to Hyun-gyu.

30
00:01:08,151 --> 00:01:09,778
I'll exchange it with Hyun-gyu.

31
00:01:09,861 --> 00:01:11,280
He's trying to funnel points to Hyun-gyu.

32
00:01:11,363 --> 00:01:13,115
-I'll exchange it with Hyun-gyu.
-…with Hyun-gyu.

33
00:01:13,198 --> 00:01:14,157
I'll exchange it with Hyun-gyu.

34
00:01:14,241 --> 00:01:15,534
So we're taking Hyun-min down?

35
00:01:15,617 --> 00:01:16,618
Last but not least, John Park.

36
00:01:16,702 --> 00:01:17,536
Hyun-min, please.

37
00:01:18,036 --> 00:01:19,746
They did it. I lost.

38
00:01:19,830 --> 00:01:23,208
<i>Oh Hyun-min is the eighth player</i>
<i>to be eliminated.</i>

39
00:01:24,376 --> 00:01:25,877
Goodness. What are you doing here?

40
00:01:25,961 --> 00:01:27,421
Through the exile zone match…

41
00:01:27,504 --> 00:01:29,172
-Elimination is unavoidable?
-Yes, to make space for the next person.

42
00:01:29,256 --> 00:01:30,966
<i>The fourth exile zone match is</i>

43
00:01:31,049 --> 00:01:32,467
<i>Loop Fence Puzzle.</i>

44
00:01:32,551 --> 00:01:34,303
<i>Farewell, Stella Jang.</i>

45
00:01:34,386 --> 00:01:36,138
We'll make sure your legacy lives on!

46
00:01:36,221 --> 00:01:38,223
<i>JAE JAE, the second queen</i>
<i>of the exile zone.</i>

47
00:01:38,307 --> 00:01:41,518
<i>In today's prison match,</i>
<i>one player will be eliminated</i>

48
00:01:41,601 --> 00:01:43,353
<i>and leave </i>The Devil's Plan.

49
00:01:43,437 --> 00:01:46,148
If we keep passing it to XITSUH
until he gets it wrong…

50
00:01:46,231 --> 00:01:47,649
Looks like I'm gonna be very popular.

51
00:01:47,733 --> 00:01:50,861
<i>We will now begin the third prison match,</i>
<i>Piggy Bank.</i>

52
00:01:50,944 --> 00:01:52,529
Who would you like to
pass the piggy bank to?

53
00:01:52,613 --> 00:01:54,614
-I'll give it to XITSUH.
-I'll pass it to XITSUH.

54
00:01:59,036 --> 00:02:00,245
Hyun-gyu, are you okay?

55
00:02:01,872 --> 00:02:03,915
<i>That concludes the prison match.</i>

56
00:02:03,999 --> 00:02:05,751
"The sum of God's numbers is zero"?

57
00:02:05,834 --> 00:02:08,587
-We concluded they're all equal.
-Isn't that a magic square?

58
00:02:10,005 --> 00:02:10,922
It's time!

59
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:12,674
I hear the bird.

60
00:02:12,758 --> 00:02:13,675
No!

61
00:02:14,301 --> 00:02:15,135
I covered it!

62
00:02:16,345 --> 00:02:17,179
Something's happening.

63
00:02:17,262 --> 00:02:19,014
There really is a black hole
at the end of the path.

64
00:02:19,097 --> 00:02:20,641
-Good luck!
-You got this!

65
00:02:20,724 --> 00:02:21,683
<i>Ha Seok-jin.</i>

66
00:02:22,309 --> 00:02:25,020
<i>You have failed God's test.</i>

67
00:02:25,103 --> 00:02:26,521
<i>Today's main match</i>

68
00:02:26,605 --> 00:02:29,024
<i>-will feature a special guest.</i>
-It's ORBIT.

69
00:02:30,067 --> 00:02:32,402
<i>Today's main match is Auction Bingo.</i>

70
00:02:32,486 --> 00:02:34,529
I need to help the prisoners.

71
00:02:34,613 --> 00:02:36,531
<i>Please select your shape.</i>

72
00:02:36,615 --> 00:02:38,241
You really need to shut down
the triangle bid this time.

73
00:02:38,325 --> 00:02:39,451
Yeah, I'm planning to.

74
00:02:39,534 --> 00:02:41,078
<i>Here is the winning bid for each shape.</i>

75
00:02:41,161 --> 00:02:42,454
The winning bid for the triangle
was two won?

76
00:02:42,537 --> 00:02:43,830
ORBIT didn't block him.

77
00:02:43,914 --> 00:02:46,458
Taking down Dong-min was never my goal.

78
00:02:46,541 --> 00:02:48,418
Making a specific person the winner
was never my goal either.

79
00:02:48,502 --> 00:02:51,713
But you just made Dong-min the winner.

80
00:02:52,756 --> 00:02:54,091
I'm so pissed off.

81
00:02:54,174 --> 00:02:56,093
<i>Round 6 will now begin.</i>

82
00:02:56,176 --> 00:02:58,512
<i>Please select your shape.</i>

83
00:02:58,595 --> 00:03:01,264
How can I when everyone else is?
I still have one more round.

84
00:03:01,348 --> 00:03:03,392
Really? You'll be done for
if this is another lie.

85
00:03:03,475 --> 00:03:04,893
ORBIT said he's going all in next round,
not now.

86
00:03:04,976 --> 00:03:05,977
I'll let you take it.

87
00:03:06,061 --> 00:03:07,687
Then you'll be eliminated.

88
00:03:07,771 --> 00:03:08,605
It's fine.

89
00:03:08,688 --> 00:03:12,192
Two one-won coins, two two-won coins,
and one ten-won coin.

90
00:03:12,275 --> 00:03:13,318
Twenty-three won.

91
00:03:14,903 --> 00:03:16,988
<i>Kim Dong-jae, the lowest-ranked player,</i>

92
00:03:17,072 --> 00:03:19,074
<i>is the tenth player to be eliminated.</i>

93
00:03:19,157 --> 00:03:21,201
I'm so embarrassed to go back home.

94
00:03:21,993 --> 00:03:22,828
Where are we?

95
00:03:22,911 --> 00:03:24,496
<i>The fifth exile zone match is</i>

96
00:03:24,579 --> 00:03:25,872
<i>Symmetrical Puzzle.</i>

97
00:03:25,956 --> 00:03:28,333
<i>-Farewell, Oh Hyun-min.</i>
-Okay.

98
00:03:28,417 --> 00:03:32,754
JAE JAE, just think of it
as filling one row with one to seven,

99
00:03:32,838 --> 00:03:34,047
and then pushing it up incrementally.

100
00:03:34,131 --> 00:03:36,341
<i>Jang Dong-min,</i>
<i>who will you use the alliance token on?</i>

101
00:03:36,425 --> 00:03:38,135
I'll be giving this to XITSUH.

102
00:03:38,218 --> 00:03:39,761
I'd like to use the salvation token.

103
00:03:39,845 --> 00:03:42,431
<i>XITSUH will be going to prison.</i>

104
00:03:42,514 --> 00:03:44,391
<i>The Devil's Plan</i> is so fun!

105
00:03:44,474 --> 00:03:47,352
<i>Today's prison match is Wall Go II.</i>

106
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:51,314
<i>XITSUH has secured his survival.</i>

107
00:03:51,398 --> 00:03:52,899
Next, John Park.

108
00:03:52,983 --> 00:03:53,900
Well, that's it then.

109
00:03:53,984 --> 00:03:58,029
<i>Yurisa is the 11th player</i>
<i>to be eliminated from </i>The Devil's Plan.

110
00:03:58,113 --> 00:04:01,283
It's my turn
to take on that hidden stage tomorrow.

111
00:04:02,117 --> 00:04:03,201
Okay!

112
00:04:06,830 --> 00:04:07,914
-Finally!
-There it is!

113
00:04:07,998 --> 00:04:09,166
It's approaching!

114
00:04:09,249 --> 00:04:11,042
-It's finally my turn.
-That's insane.

115
00:04:11,126 --> 00:04:12,919
This is actually insane.

116
00:04:13,003 --> 00:04:14,838
God watches over us through the sun.

117
00:04:14,921 --> 00:04:16,631
I can see the black hole waiting for me.

118
00:04:16,715 --> 00:04:17,883
I'm off!

119
00:04:39,237 --> 00:04:41,281
<i>There were exactly 49.</i>

120
00:04:41,865 --> 00:04:43,575
<i>I was genuinely stunned.</i>

121
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:46,328
It's 49?

122
00:04:46,411 --> 00:04:47,954
Damn, it's 49.

123
00:04:51,583 --> 00:04:53,585
<i>A thousand different thoughts</i>
<i>ran through my head.</i>

124
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:57,214
I pictured Seok-jin having a meltdown.

125
00:04:57,297 --> 00:04:59,716
Oh my God!

126
00:04:59,799 --> 00:05:02,511
<i>He must've looked just like me</i>
<i>at the start.</i>

127
00:05:08,725 --> 00:05:09,601
One hour.

128
00:05:13,730 --> 00:05:15,148
This can't be it though.

129
00:05:15,774 --> 00:05:16,733
Eight.

130
00:05:16,816 --> 00:05:17,901
I've tried this before.

131
00:05:18,652 --> 00:05:20,028
One is the starting point, right?

132
00:05:20,111 --> 00:05:22,489
From the starting point,

133
00:05:22,572 --> 00:05:24,574
it's 7N+1 straight through.

134
00:05:24,658 --> 00:05:26,117
<i>So I placed</i>

135
00:05:27,035 --> 00:05:29,663
<i>the tiles diagonally.</i>

136
00:05:30,455 --> 00:05:31,665
Forty-three.

137
00:05:33,041 --> 00:05:35,418
Let's do this.

138
00:05:36,503 --> 00:05:38,964
Maybe I can rearrange things
to bring the smaller numbers down.

139
00:05:45,637 --> 00:05:46,471
Thirty-two.

140
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:48,723
Thirty-nine.

141
00:05:51,851 --> 00:05:54,104
Oh, I forgot to include 48 earlier.

142
00:05:57,232 --> 00:05:58,066
Let's see.

143
00:05:59,317 --> 00:06:02,237
I've placed all the numbers
by the remainder diagonally.

144
00:06:03,113 --> 00:06:04,531
But it doesn't work.

145
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:07,367
There's no way it can with that top row.

146
00:06:08,118 --> 00:06:09,411
How should I rearrange this?

147
00:06:09,995 --> 00:06:11,329
But earlier, Dong-jae said…

148
00:06:11,413 --> 00:06:13,498
Isn't the secret
planting 25 in the center?

149
00:06:17,877 --> 00:06:20,171
Start by planting 25 in the center?

150
00:06:20,255 --> 00:06:22,882
But how, when one is here?

151
00:06:25,385 --> 00:06:27,804
<i>Since 25 is the median of 1 through 49,</i>

152
00:06:27,887 --> 00:06:29,723
<i>it has to land in the center, right?</i>

153
00:06:29,806 --> 00:06:31,891
But 26 ends up there if you work this way.

154
00:06:31,975 --> 00:06:36,187
<i>To get 25 to land in the center,</i>

155
00:06:36,271 --> 00:06:38,648
<i>I had to try out a different layout.</i>

156
00:06:39,899 --> 00:06:40,984
Damn it.

157
00:06:43,278 --> 00:06:44,487
What a headache.

158
00:06:47,657 --> 00:06:49,409
Okay, let's switch the diagonal direction.

159
00:06:50,243 --> 00:06:52,370
There has to be a reason
one is the starting point.

160
00:06:55,332 --> 00:06:57,042
But 25 has to land in the center.

161
00:06:58,668 --> 00:06:59,961
Then maybe

162
00:07:00,795 --> 00:07:03,465
I should slide the numbers over.

163
00:07:03,548 --> 00:07:04,883
Let's try that.

164
00:07:11,181 --> 00:07:12,015
Okay.

165
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:14,809
All right. I should move things this way.

166
00:07:15,435 --> 00:07:17,520
Then this one goes here,

167
00:07:18,521 --> 00:07:19,981
and this one comes here.

168
00:07:20,774 --> 00:07:25,779
Then, the same thing here.

169
00:07:29,616 --> 00:07:30,909
Now, 25.

170
00:07:30,992 --> 00:07:32,118
Here it is.

171
00:07:32,202 --> 00:07:34,037
Okay, 25 is at the center.

172
00:07:34,871 --> 00:07:35,747
There's 25.

173
00:07:36,331 --> 00:07:39,084
<i>I switched the direction of the diagonal.</i>

174
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:41,252
<i>So it went 1, 8, 15, 22.</i>

175
00:07:41,336 --> 00:07:42,504
That's 42.

176
00:07:43,129 --> 00:07:44,089
That's 49.

177
00:07:44,172 --> 00:07:45,632
Wow, 49.

178
00:07:45,715 --> 00:07:47,175
I got chills. So 49 goes there.

179
00:07:48,593 --> 00:07:50,512
So having 25 here is the right way to go.

180
00:07:51,554 --> 00:07:52,389
That's 13.

181
00:07:53,139 --> 00:07:54,099
That's 41.

182
00:07:54,766 --> 00:07:56,559
That's 48. Good.

183
00:07:57,185 --> 00:07:58,144
That's 19.

184
00:08:00,939 --> 00:08:02,315
That's 29.

185
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:04,609
That's 30, so I need 37.

186
00:08:04,693 --> 00:08:05,819
Damn, that works.

187
00:08:07,278 --> 00:08:08,279
That's 44.

188
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:10,323
Okay, let's see.

189
00:08:11,491 --> 00:08:13,159
So 1 plus 9 is 10.

190
00:08:13,243 --> 00:08:14,703
Plus 17, so 27.

191
00:08:15,328 --> 00:08:17,455
Then, 27 plus 25.

192
00:08:17,539 --> 00:08:18,832
Then, you get 126.

193
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:21,209
Add 49… No way, that's 175.

194
00:08:21,292 --> 00:08:22,961
So all the columns add up to 175.

195
00:08:23,545 --> 00:08:25,964
But not all the rows,
especially this top row.

196
00:08:30,552 --> 00:08:31,720
It's so hot in here.

197
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:37,016
JAE JAE, just think of it
as filling one row with one to seven,

198
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:38,435
and then pushing it up incrementally.

199
00:08:39,102 --> 00:08:40,103
Okay.

200
00:08:41,438 --> 00:08:43,273
What did Hyun-min mean by pushing it up?

201
00:08:43,356 --> 00:08:44,941
It feels like that should do it.

202
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:46,651
It works vertically.

203
00:08:48,319 --> 00:08:51,364
It adds up vertically,
so maybe I can push up starting with two.

204
00:08:52,657 --> 00:08:57,829
<i>The sum of the columns came out to 175.</i>

205
00:08:57,912 --> 00:09:02,250
Something had to shift
for the sum of the rows

206
00:09:02,333 --> 00:09:06,171
and the diagonal sums to match,
but the columns had to stay as is.

207
00:09:06,254 --> 00:09:08,465
Then I remembered Hyun-min saying,

208
00:09:08,548 --> 00:09:10,383
"Just push it up incrementally."

209
00:09:10,467 --> 00:09:13,803
<i>I had to move</i>
<i>the bigger numbers up somehow.</i>

210
00:09:14,763 --> 00:09:16,264
Start with two?

211
00:09:17,223 --> 00:09:18,683
The bigger numbers need to go up.

212
00:09:19,559 --> 00:09:21,102
Then…

213
00:09:25,190 --> 00:09:26,065
Like so.

214
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:33,782
It'll still work vertically.

215
00:09:35,992 --> 00:09:36,951
Hold on.

216
00:09:38,369 --> 00:09:39,621
Push this one up two squares.

217
00:09:41,039 --> 00:09:43,541
Then this goes down here.

218
00:09:46,461 --> 00:09:47,629
This goes up here.

219
00:09:49,089 --> 00:09:50,840
I hope this is what he meant.

220
00:09:51,591 --> 00:09:54,302
"Incrementally" must mean
one more per column, right?

221
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:56,221
One more.

222
00:09:56,304 --> 00:09:57,972
This then goes here.

223
00:09:58,056 --> 00:10:00,850
That gets pushed up once.
This gets pushed up twice.

224
00:10:02,227 --> 00:10:03,311
So this goes here.

225
00:10:04,395 --> 00:10:07,732
Then the smaller numbers
end up here and here.

226
00:10:07,816 --> 00:10:09,776
I pushed these up by one square each

227
00:10:09,859 --> 00:10:12,987
and these by two squares each,
so it's three squares each this time.

228
00:10:13,613 --> 00:10:16,157
How many do I need to pull out? Three.

229
00:10:23,665 --> 00:10:24,833
There we go.

230
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:26,876
There.

231
00:10:32,048 --> 00:10:33,883
Since this side got shifted up…

232
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:42,100
<i>I got stuck again at that point.</i>

233
00:10:42,183 --> 00:10:44,310
<i>I moved up the smaller numbers</i>
<i>on the right side.</i>

234
00:10:44,394 --> 00:10:47,772
If I had done the same for the left side,

235
00:10:47,856 --> 00:10:50,942
all the smaller numbers
would've made their way up

236
00:10:51,025 --> 00:10:54,028
to decrease the sum of the row again.

237
00:10:54,112 --> 00:10:56,406
So the columns on the left
had to be moved down.

238
00:10:56,489 --> 00:10:58,533
This side has to come down
for the sum of the diagonal.

239
00:11:06,291 --> 00:11:08,126
I pushed this column down by one,

240
00:11:08,209 --> 00:11:09,752
so this has to be pushed down by two.

241
00:11:09,836 --> 00:11:14,215
Then I need to take these out

242
00:11:14,841 --> 00:11:16,009
and push them down.

243
00:11:18,678 --> 00:11:20,680
You need to go down for the sums to match.

244
00:11:20,763 --> 00:11:22,515
And these two end up on top.

245
00:11:25,977 --> 00:11:27,353
To move three squares down,

246
00:11:28,438 --> 00:11:29,814
I need to remove four tiles.

247
00:11:29,898 --> 00:11:32,275
Why is God's room so hot?

248
00:11:35,194 --> 00:11:36,279
This comes down,

249
00:11:36,362 --> 00:11:38,114
and these three go up.

250
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:44,871
Okay, let's see.

251
00:11:44,954 --> 00:11:45,955
That's 30.

252
00:11:46,581 --> 00:11:47,582
Please tell me this is right.

253
00:12:06,184 --> 00:12:07,185
Is this it?

254
00:12:08,728 --> 00:12:11,147
